  "implemented": [
    "PrivateControl authenticates shielded connect/status through the same explicitly accepted CA/SPKI-pinned HTTPS client; no public status fallback",
    "AcceptedPrivatePlan keeps pool/source/operator/generation/tariff, finite class caps and quote ceiling explicit; the ceiling is not withdrawable channel OCT",
    "PreparedPrivateClient persists its signed connection watermark before network access and refuses a missing purchased floor before UDP/TUN startup",
    "PrivatePaymentClient opens the existing WireGuard and kernel TUN path only after rechecking private admission; it owns no native payer key and submits no payment",
    "Private transport journals seal the complete state with XChaCha20-Poly1305 and a scoped key derived separately from the receipt signing secret",
    "Existing single-writer leases, atomic/fsynced installation, replacement detection, poisoned-write handling and conservative interrupted IO recovery are reused",
    "Signed private snapshots retain monotonic funding, purchase, delivery-slot, connection and canonical-clock observations across reconnect without increasing local caps",
    "The public and private clients share the conservative packet handoff driver, journal worker ownership and shutdown supervisor",
    "Private summaries expose byte counters without misrepresenting a quote ceiling as an available native balance"
  ],
